<h5>General Settings</h5>
<p>App name, company name, logo (also favicon), timezone, and region. Admin: <code>/admin/system/general</code> (administrators).</p>
<p><strong>Reading (homepage &amp; blog):</strong> Choose a static front page or latest posts, pick which published page is the homepage, and set posts per page (paginated blog). WordPress-style <code>Settings → Reading</code> equivalent in General settings.</p>
<p><strong>Discussion:</strong> Enable comments on posts, require moderation, name/email requirements, and show the sidebar widget area on public pages.</p>
<p><strong>Permalinks:</strong> Custom URL patterns for pages (default <code>/p/slug</code> or plain <code>/slug</code>) and posts (default <code>/blog/slug</code>, plain, year/month, or category-based). Default routes always remain available.</p>
<p><strong>Public site theme:</strong> Color presets (Default, Ocean, Forest, Sunset, Violet, Slate, Rose, Custom), accent color, typography, corner radius, site content width, <strong>blog listing width</strong>, default light/dark mode, header style, optional light/dark toggle, and <strong>Preview on live site</strong> (opens <code>/?theme_preview=1</code> with unsaved settings). Live mini-preview on the General page. Settings apply to the public site, blog listing, and admin login/2FA pages.</p>
<p><strong>Site-wide SEO &amp; LLM:</strong> Default meta description, title suffix, default Open Graph image, Twitter handle, Facebook/LinkedIn URLs (Schema.org <code>sameAs</code>), Google verification, locale, keywords, LLM site summary, and toggles for <code>/sitemap.xml</code>, <code>/feed.xml</code> (RSS), JSON exports (<code>/site.json</code>, <code>/blog.json</code>), <code>/llms.txt</code>, and allowing AI crawlers in <code>robots.txt</code>. Per-page and per-post SEO fields override these defaults.</p>
